|           Status / Error          |                                                Root Cause                                                |                                                                                                    Debugging & Resolution Steps                                                                                                   |
|:---------------------------------:|:--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------:|:---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------:|
| CreateContainerConfigError        | The Pod specification referenced a ConfigMap or Secret that does not exist in the active namespace.      | 1. Run kubectl describe pod <pod-name> to identify the missing resource key. 2. Check existing resources via kubectl get cm,secret. 3. Apply the missing manifest; the kubelet reconciles and starts the container automatically. |
| container not found ("nginx")     | Running kubectl exec against a Pod that is terminating, restarting, or failed during container creation. | Target only healthy pods using field selectors: kubectl get pods --field-selector=status.phase=Running.                                                                                                                           |
| Endpoints is deprecated in v1.33+ | Monolithic v1.Endpoints objects do not scale efficiently in large clusters.                              | Inspect modern endpoint slices chunked by the EndpointSlice Controller: kubectl get endpointslice[cite: 2].                                                                                                                       |
| Protection Rules                  | Cannot pause itself for manual review natively without custom script polling.                            | Natively enforces Required Reviewers (Manual Gates), deployment wait timers, and branch restrictions.                                                                                                                             |